Tether Agent is inspired by Hermes Agent from Nous Research:
https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent

Tether Agent is a new program in Go, but some parts are ports of Hermes Agent
code from Python to Go. Some prompts, rules, patterns, and test cases are
copied from Hermes Agent. These parts include:

- The secret redaction rules (internal/security/redact.go, from agent/redact.py).
- The dangerous-command rules and the approval flow (internal/security/,
  from tools/approval.py).
- The threat rules of the skill guard (internal/skills/guard_patterns.go and
  internal/skills/testdata/guard_golden.json, from tools/skills_guard.py).
- The prompts for child agents, background reviews, and context compaction
  (internal/agent/, internal/ctxmgr/).
- The Telegram message format, stream, group gate, and media delivery rules
  (internal/telegram/, from gateway/).
- The fuzzy match of the patch tool (internal/tools/patch.go).
- Test cases from the Hermes Agent test suite.

Comments in the source code that name "Hermes" point to the origin of a rule
or a text. Hermes Agent is distributed under the MIT License below.

